            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Patch includes test to highlight broken EgdeNGramTokenFilter and NGramTokenFilter. Fixes for both.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tfeak",
            "name": "tfeak",
            "key": "tfeak",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Todd Feak",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-12-15T22:41:19.577+0000",
          "updated": "2008-12-15T22:41:19.577+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12410617/comment/12658308",
          "id": "12658308",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "patch looks good ... the one question i have is whether the fix meets user expectations: the patch as posted \"skips\" any input tokens that are shorter then the minimum ngram length ... is that what most people will expect, or will people expect shorter tokens to be passed through?\n\nie: should \"min\" be the minimum token size produced by the filters (a hard min), or should it be the minimum ngram size produced by the filter (a soft min)?\n\neither way this patch is an improvement, i'm just wondering what we want to define the semantics to be (or if we want to make an additional option for this)",
          "updateAuthor": {
